{"id": "EUVD-2026-103839", "enisaUuid": "3f3a689e-8045-37ca-a450-a0d31f3636fa", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ntty: vcc: hold port lock when clearing tty pointer in vcc_cleanup\n\nvcc_cleanup() sets port->tty to NULL without holding port->lock, racing\nwith vcc_event() LDC callbacks that read port->tty under port->lock and\nthen use tty->port. This can cause a use-after-free when the callback\ndereferences tty->port after cleanup has already destroyed and freed it.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:47:40", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:56:29", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/57753441ef84bee3bf0e9ee1e3778d119c44aa32", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/88f6ecb058801e9ce7b9aabc966530118d7cd53c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/821050631750e982007c0856c119346edba51cae", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1a9fb9eaeb69b1f6c00bed09289a33d9fe1e7ae4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/03b49c991abb8d021ca6fe51cd173447236b0552"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98754", "GHSA-phxc-9rqx-x894"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "013a7262-b2f0-3c6d-8c72-bd08fcce9829", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <1a9fb9eaeb69b1f6c00bed09289a33d9fe1e7ae4"}, {"id": "0792ad12-aeef-3689-ad59-1eb44f5244c4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "3a307b5b-402c-33ee-b325-6a7778f45ff6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <88f6ecb058801e9ce7b9aabc966530118d7cd53c"}, {"id": "44b3abfb-447d-3af1-8aee-e52f54f36cde", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "47fb4016-7496-31fe-b21c-6dedd4334ccd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321ca